Enforcement Decree of the National Aviation Museum Act

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the National Aviation Museum Act and matters necessary for its implementation.

Article 2 (Museum Materials)
"Items prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5 (1) 2 of the National Aviation Museum Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means tangible and intangible materials that meet all of the following requirements. In such cases, intangible materials shall be limited to materials that can be expressed in codes, characters, voices, sounds, images, or similar forms.
1. They shall have academic or artistic value warranting collection, preservation, management, investigation, research, or exhibition by the National Aviation Museum under Article 2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Museum") to achieve its purpose of establishment and conduct its business;
2. They shall concern history, folklore, arts, science, technology, industry, or other matters related to aviation culture and the aviation industry.

Article 3 (Revenue-Generating Activities)
(1) Revenue-generating activities under Article 5 (1) 8 of the Act shall be as follows:
1. Admission to the Museum and viewing of exhibition halls, etc.;
2. Rental of Museum facilities;
3. Production and sale of Museum-related souvenirs, publications, periodicals, etc.;
4. Distribution of educational programs developed by the Museum;
5. Advertising using Museum facilities;
6. Installation and operation of aviation-related experience facilities;
7. Other activities that the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems necessary to raise funds for conducting the Museum's business.
(2) Where the Museum intends to obtain approval for revenue-generating activities pursuant to Article 5 (2) of the Act, it shall submit the following documents to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport following a resolution of the board of directors under Article 10 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "board of directors"):
1. An application for approval of revenue-generating activities;
2. A plan for revenue-generating activities;
3. A projected income statement and accompanying schedules.
(3) Where the Museum intends to conduct approved revenue-generating activities, it shall report the business plan for the following business year to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport by October 1 of the preceding year: Provided, That this shall not apply where a plan for revenue-generating activities has been submitted during the relevant year to obtain approval for those activities pursuant to paragraph (2).
(4) After the end of a business year, the Museum shall submit a performance report and statement of settlement of accounts for its revenue-generating activities to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport by March 31 of the following business year.
(5) The Museum shall establish separate accounts to manage revenue and expenditure arising from the operation of revenue-generating activities.

Article 4 (Submission of Budget Requests for Contributions, Etc.)
(1) Where the Museum intends to request a contribution from the State pursuant to Article 11 (2) of the Act, it shall submit a budget request for the contribution to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport by April 30 each year, accompanied by the following documents:
1. A business plan for the following business year;
2. A projected statement of financial position, a projected income statement, and accompanying schedules for the following business year;
3. Other materials explaining the details of the requested contribution.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport finds a budget request under paragraph (1) appropriate, the Minister shall prepare a draft budget reflecting the request and shall notify the Museum when the budget for the contribution is finalized.

Article 5 (Payment of Contributions)
(1) Where the Museum intends to receive payment of a contribution pursuant to Article 11 (2) of the Act, it shall submit the following documents to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport:
1. An application for payment of a contribution;
2. A quarterly business plan;
3. A quarterly budget execution plan.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport finds the contents of the quarterly business plan and quarterly budget execution plan submitted under paragraph (1) appropriate, the Minister shall pay the contribution accordingly.
(3) The Museum shall establish a separate account to manage a contribution paid under paragraph (2) and shall use it only for the purposes specified in the quarterly business plan and quarterly budget execution plan under paragraph (1).
(4) Where the Museum receives a contribution under paragraph (2), it shall report its quarterly execution results to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport within 20 days after the end of the relevant quarter.

Article 6 (Procedures for Accepting Donations, Etc.)
(1) Where the Museum receives a donation of money or other property from an individual, corporation, or organization pursuant to Article 11 (3) of the Act, it shall issue a receipt to the donor: Provided, That a receipt need not be issued where the donation is anonymous or the donor cannot be identified.
(2) Where a donor specifies the purpose for which money or other property donated under paragraph (1) (hereinafter referred to as "donated money and property") is to be used, the Museum shall use the donated money and property only for that purpose: Provided, That where special reasons make it difficult to use the donated money and property for the purpose specified by the donor, it may be used for another purpose with the donor's consent.
(3) The Museum shall keep records of the receipt and use of donated money and property and other relevant matters and make those records available for inspection by donors.
(4) The Museum shall establish a separate account to manage donated money.

Article 7 (Submission of Business Plans, Etc.)
(1) Where the Director of the Museum (hereinafter referred to as the "Director") intends to obtain approval of a business plan and budget pursuant to Article 12 (2) of the Act, the Director shall submit the business plan and budget for the following business year to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport by December 15 each year.
(2) The business plan under paragraph (1) shall include the following matters for each project:
1. Project objectives;
2. Project details;
3. Intended beneficiaries;
4. Project costs;
5. Other matters necessary to clarify the contents of the business plan.
(3) The budget under paragraph (1) shall include the following:
1. General budget provisions;
2. A projected statement of financial position, a projected income statement, and accompanying schedules;
3. A funding plan;
4. Other matters necessary to clarify the contents of the budget.
(4) Where the Director intends to amend an approved business plan and budget, the Director shall submit the following documents to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport:
1. A document stating the details of and reasons for the amendment;
2. A business plan and budget reflecting the amendment.

Article 8 (Submission of Statements of Settlement, etc.)
The Director shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport a report on business performance and a statement of settlement of revenue and expenditure for each fiscal year pursuant to Article 12 (3) of the Act, accompanied by the following documents:
1. Financial statements for the relevant fiscal year (including an audit opinion of a certified public accountant or an accounting corporation under Article 23 of the Certified Public Accountant Act) and their accompanying documents;
2. A table comparing the business plan for the relevant fiscal year with its implementation performance;
3. A copy of the minutes of the meeting of the board of directors concerning its resolution on the statement of settlement of revenue and expenditure;
4. Other documents necessary to clarify the details of the settlement of accounts.

Article 9 (Application for Approval to Borrow Funds)
Where the Museum intends to obtain approval to borrow funds pursuant to Article 13 of the Act, it shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application for approval to borrow funds, accompanied by the following documents:
1. A document specifying the lender, the reasons for borrowing, the terms of borrowing, and the amount to be borrowed;
2. A document specifying the method and deadline for repayment of the borrowed funds;
3. A document specifying other matters necessary for borrowing and repayment of the funds.

Article 10 (Disposition of Surplus)
The Museum shall first apply the surplus for each business year to repayment of its debts and shall carry forward any remaining surplus to the following business year or use it to carry out the Museum's projects.

Article 11 (Composition and Operation of Supporters' Association)
(1) The Museum's supporters' association under Article 14 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "supporters' association") shall consist of individuals or corporations intending to support the Museum's projects.
(2) Members of the supporters' association may provide money, property, academic materials, etc. to support the Museum through the supporters' association. In such cases, members of the supporters' association may designate a specific project among the Museum's projects to support.
(3) The Director may distribute publications issued by the Museum to members of the supporters' association free of charge or exempt such members from admission fees, viewing fees, or facility use fees.
(4) Where the Director receives money, property, academic materials, etc. from the supporters' association pursuant to paragraph (2), the Director shall notify the supporters' association of the details of their use by December 31 of each year.

Article 12 (Entrustment and Management of Museum Materials)
(1) Where damage, breakage, or other loss occurs to museum materials the management of which has been entrusted by the State pursuant to Article 15 (1) of the Act, the Director shall report that fact to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport without delay.
(2) The Director shall obtain prior approval from the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to undertake large-scale repairs or maintenance that alter the original form of museum materials the management of which has been entrusted by the State pursuant to Article 15 (1) of the Act: Provided, That in an emergency, the Director shall take the minimum necessary measures and then report the details thereof to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport without delay.
(3) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport entrusts the management of museum materials pursuant to Article 15 (1) of the Act, the Minister may provide support for expenses necessary for their preservation, treatment, and management within budgetary limits.

Article 13 (Requests for Dispatch of Public Officials, etc.)
(1) Where the Director intends to obtain approval from the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to request that the head of a relevant administrative agency or educational institution dispatch public officials or other personnel belonging to that agency or institution pursuant to Article 17 (1) of the Act, the Director shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport a request for approval of dispatch specifying the following matters:
1. Reasons for requesting the dispatch;
2. Period of dispatch;
3. Number of personnel to be dispatched;
4. Fields of expertise and qualification requirements of the personnel to be dispatched.
(2) Public officials or other personnel dispatched to the Museum pursuant to Article 17 (2) of the Act shall comply with the service regulations, etc. prescribed by the Director during the period of dispatch.
(3) The Museum may pay allowances to public officials or other personnel dispatched pursuant to Article 17 of the Act in accordance with the standards prescribed by the Museum's articles of incorporation: Provided, That allowances paid to dispatched personnel who are public officials shall not exceed the standards applicable to the following categories:
1. National public officials: The standards prescribed by the Minister of Personnel Management pursuant to Article 41 (8) of the Decree on the Appointment of Public Officials;
2. Local public officials: The standards prescribed by the Minister of the Interior and Safety pursuant to Article 27-2 (6) of the Decree on the Appointment of Local Public Officials.

Article 14 (Conduct of Operational Evaluations)
(1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall conduct an operational evaluation under Article 18 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "operational evaluation") every three years.
(2) The criteria for an operational evaluation shall be as follows:
1. Evaluation of the Museum's management status: The degree of accountable management and work efficiency, the appropriateness of budgetary, organizational, and human resource management, etc.;
2. Evaluation of the performance of projects, such as the collection, preservation, management, and exhibition of museum materials: The extent to which the infrastructure for collecting museum materials has been expanded, the results of implementing the Museum's basic operating plan and medium- and long-term development plan, etc.;
3. Evaluation of services provided to the public in connection with the Museum's operations: Levels of customer satisfaction and public perception, performance in improving services, etc.
(3) To conduct an operational evaluation, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall prepare evaluation guidelines specifying the basic direction, criteria, subjects, schedule, etc. of the operational evaluation and notify the Museum thereof no later than three months before the date of the operational evaluation.

